  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041740",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-49570",
      "knowledge_point_id": "abad9fa9-b426-50aa-aaa7-d472ea974f98",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining Values for Which a Geometric Sequence Converges: Rearrangement Required",
      "problem": "Consider the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{n+3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{x}^{n+3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{n}\\cdot {x}^{3}}{{3}^{n}\\cdot x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{x}{3})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe see that this is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Since $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive. So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{x}{3}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,0<x\\le 3.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x>0",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0<x\\le 3",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0<x\\le \\frac{1}{3}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x\\ge 3",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 9990,
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-49570",
