    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-115434",
      "knowledge_point_id": "281514e9-6e16-5b21-ba4e-503991d811c2",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Equation of a Parabola Passing Through a Given Point",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-5,2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe're told that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 25 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{25}{8})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{5}y",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}y",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{8}y",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{5}y",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{x}^{2}=\\frac{25}{2}y",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 5095,
